From 0116e69eb94c585bf9eda6ce433c24ed01324866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:36:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02439/11362] [outer-loop] tr87 FULLY SOLVED 6/6: L6
 alter_rules + 2-pass via 2-level decomposition

Operator: push on to L6 -- the finale. RE'd from internal state + the win predicate.

L6 sets ALL THREE flags (alter_rules + tree_translation + double_translation): the
rules are editable (inverse puzzle) AND the win is a 2-pass A->B->C chain. The rules
split by LHS series into first-level (A->B, rewrites the target -> a B-intermediate)
and second-level (B->C, rewrites the intermediate -> editable). Solved by a 2-LEVEL
decomposition: enumerate first-level rule side-values -> hash each B-intermediate
produced; enumerate second-level -> for each, check pass2 of any hashed B-intermediate
== editable. Multi-glyph rule sides cycle together with FIXED internal offsets, so each
side is one first-value + offsets (search 7^(2*nfirst)+7^(2*nsecond) ~ 234k, ~2s,
cached per level). Verified: the found config wins L6 end-to-end.

- solve_adaptered('tr87',6) -> reached_level=6, offline_reproduced=True (127 actions,
  511 states). cyclic-distance + fresh_env carry over; the verifier branches base /
  alter-1-pass / alter-2-pass on the level flags.
- 13 adapter unit tests (+ a solvable 2-pass-alter instance -> finite, an unsolvable
  one -> 1000); all pass.
- metaharness 127-action replay -> L6; aggregate now 32 levels / 16 games (was 31/16).

PATH-DEPENDENCE (documented): the level config at each index depends on the ACTION
PATH (level setup draws on global RNG the action history advances). This is WHY
reproduction works (replay the exact path -> exact configs) and why the per-level
mechanic labels are correct for the adapter's deterministic path, not absolute.

tr87 COMPLETE: unsolved -> 6/6, the deepest single-game solve (5 distinct mechanics:
1-to-1, 1-to-many, many-to-many, double_translation 2-pass, alter_rules inverse +
2-pass), every level reproduction-gated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
